{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.casimirX8_succ_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.casimirX8_succ_sub","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.lean#L119-L126","doc":"The Casimir differences that the fit actually used, as a ring identity:\n`C₂` at `n` and `n+1` differ by `(5/8)(3 − 2n)`, scaled here by 8. Included so\nthe `λ = 3/4` interpolation of the fitted model is checkable from the file\nrather than only from the probe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.pairSum_add_five_pairCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.pairSum_add_five_pairCount","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.lean#L112-L117","doc":"Restated as the proportionality itself: `16·S + 5·(2·C(n,2)) = 0`, so the\nratio `S / C(n,2)` is the constant `−5/8` and carries no `n`-dependence for a\ncoordination weight to inherit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.pairSum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.pairSum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.lean#L101-L110","doc":"**The two-body sum is exactly proportional to the pair count.**\n`16·S = −5·n(n−1)`, i.e. `S(n) = −(5/8)·C(n,2)` for every `n`.\n\nThis is the load-bearing statement: a two-body SU(4)-invariant interaction\nsummed over the fully antisymmetric `A`-body state contributes a *constant per\npair*, so it gives a constant coordination weight and `b₃ = 0`. The SU(4)\nCasimir cannot produce a three-body cumulant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.casimirX8_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.casimirX8_eq","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.lean#L94-L99","doc":"**The Casimir is affine in the pair count.** `8·C₂ = 15n − 5·n(n−1)`, i.e.\n`C₂([1^n]) = (15/8)·n − (5/4)·C(n,2)`. Every apparent dependence of the Casimir\non the many-body structure is carried by `n` and the pair count alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.pairSumX16","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.pairSumX16","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.lean#L90-L92","doc":"`16 · S(n)` where `S(n) = Σ_{i<j} λᵢ·λⱼ = ½(C₂([1^n]) − n·C₂(fund))` and\n`C₂(fund) = 15/8`; scaled by 16, so `16·S = 8·C₂ − 15n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.pairCountX2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.pairCountX2","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.lean#L87-L88","doc":"`2 · C(n,2) = n(n−1)`, the pair count scaled by 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.casimirX8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.casimirX8","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SU4CasimirIsAffineInPairCount.lean#L83-L85","doc":"`8 · C₂([1^n])` for the fully antisymmetric representation of SU(4), whose\nCasimir is `(5/8)·n·(4−n)`. Scaled by 8 to stay in a ring without division. ","signatureChunk":0}]}